$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 14221-01-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 76189-56-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 67-63-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM phenyl-4-methoxyphenylsulfide 4-Bromoanisole (3.35 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0
equiv), 2-propanol (30 mL), potassium hydroxide (3.47 g, 53.46 mmol, 2.0
equiv), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (154 mg, 0.134 mmol,
0.005 equiv), (S)-BINAP (166 mg., 0.267 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and
benzenethiol (2.74 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 22-24 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was
completed it was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (30 mL) which
resulted in a small exotherm (+6 °C) and formation of an oil. The
resultant mixture was allowed to stir for 1 h at 10-15 °C. Isolated the
oil, neutralized (~pH 7) and extracted with ethyl acetate washed with
water, brine and dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, concentrated to
dryness. Obtained a red oil4, 5.4 g. phenyl-4-methoxyphenylsulfide, Yield
93% m/z 216; C13H12OS requires C, 72.2; H, 5.59; S, 14.8. Found: C, 72.7;
H, 5.60; S, 15.15%; 1H NMR (400 MHz, d6-DMSO) δ 7.42 (m, 2H), 7.18 (m,
5H), 6.90 (m, 2), 3.82 (s, 3H); IR (cm-1) νmax; 1592, 1493, 1247.
