$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-(naphthalen-1-ylthio)benzaldehyde. To a stirred solution
of naphthalene-1-thiol (4.27 g, 26.71 mmol) and anhydrous Na2CO3 (3.50 g)
in dry DMF (8 mL) under nitrogen at 90 °C, 2-chlorobenzaldehyde (2.40 ml,
21.31 mmol) was slowly added. The mixture was stirred at 90 °C for 3
hours. After cooling, the reaction mixture was poured into water (20 mL)
and extracted with diethyl ether (20 mL). The extract was washed with
water (2x20 mL), dried with anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated under
vacuum. The resulting oil was triturated with hexane in an ultrasound
bath for 20 min, filtered and dried under vacuum. A yellow solid (5.03 g,
25.35 mmol, 93%). IR (cm-1): 3356w, 3056w, 2965w, 2860w, 2756w, 1695m,
1591m, 1552w, 1491m, 1447m, 1400m, 300w, 1269m, 1117w, 1060w, 1047w,
939w, 860w, 826m, 808m, 743s, 708m, 630w, 530w, 473s, 430w. 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3): δ, 7.13 (d, J= 7.5 Hz, 1H, CH (Ph)), 7.36- 7.57 (m, 4H,
CH(Ph)), 7.80-7.93 (m ,5H, CH(Ph)), 7.99 (s, 1H, CH(Ph)), 10.45 (s, 1H,
CHO). Anal.Calc. for C17H12OS (264.34): C, 77.24; H, 4.58. Found: C,
77.39; H, 4.42%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Porous Molecular Crystals by Macrocyclic Coordination Supramolecules
