$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of Silver (Z)-Enethiolate 1a with 2,4-Dinitrochlorobenzene in
the Presence of Bu4NI. To a stirred solution of Bu4NI (17.4 mg, 0.047
mmol) in dichloromethane (2 mL) was added silver (Z)-enethiolate 1a (13.2
mg, 0.047 mmol) at room temperature under nitrogen in the dark and the
resulting yellow solution was stirred for 0.5 h. A solution of
1-chloro-2,4-dinitrobenzene (7.9 mg, 0.039 mmol) in dichloromethane (1
mL) was added and the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 48 h.
After addition of water, the mixture was extracted with dichloromethane.
The combined organic phase was washed with water, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under an aspirator vacuum to give an
oil, which was purified by preparative TLC (ethyl acetate:hexane = 6:4)
to yield (Z)-1-decenyl 2,4-dinitrophenyl sulfide (12.2 mg, 93%) as a
yellow oil: IR (neat) 3105, 2926, 2855, 1594, 1522, 1339, 1051, 917, 833,
736 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.09 (d, J = 2.6 Hz, 1H), 8.34 (dd, J
= 8.8, 2.6 Hz, 1H), 7.66 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.45 (dt, J = 9.1, 6.9 Hz,
1H), 6.19 (d, J = 9.1 Hz, 1H), 2.39 (q, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 1.51-1.41 (m,
2H), 1.38-1.17 (m, 10H), 0.87 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 3H); MS m/z (relative
intensity) 338 (M+, 57), 239 (32), 183 (100), 137 (66), 95 (32), 83 (48):
HRMS calcd for C16H22O4N2S (M+) 338.1300, found 338.1291.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Silver Technology for Stabilization of Simple (Z)-Enethiols:
Stereoselective Synthesis and Reaction of Silver (Z)-Enethiolates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Ochiai, Masahito; Hirobe, Masaya; Miyamoto, Kazunori
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(28), 9046-9047

