$DATUM The potassium thiolate 7 (150 mg, 0.37 mmol) in 3.0 mL of DMF was heated
with K2CO3 (76 mg, 0.55 mmol) and 4,5-dichloro-2-nitroaniline (76 mg,
0.37 mmol) at 70 °C for 3 h. Reaction was then quenched with water after
cooling to room temperature. The yellow precipitates were collected
through filtration, washed with water, and dried in a vacuum oven to give
the nitro compound 11 (170 mg, 0.34 mmol, 93%).
