$DATUM 4-fluorophenyl-3'-tolylsulfide 3-Bromotoluene (2.28 mL, 18.77 mmol, 1.0
equiv), 2-propanol (20 mL), potassium hydroxide (2.44 g, 37.54 mmol, 2.0
equiv), tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (217 mg,, 0.188 mmol,
0.01 equiv), (S)-BINAP (117 mg, 0.188 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and 4-
fluorobenzenethiol (2.0 mL, 18.77 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 6 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was completed it
was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (20 mL) which resulted in
formation of an oil. The mixture was allowed to granulate for 1 h at
10-15 °C and then filtered. The filtrate was acidified (pH 2) using conc.
HCl. and extracted using dichloromethane, washed with 50% aqueous sodium
hydroxide, filtered through cotton and concentrated to an oil. Placed
under high vacuum to obtain 3.8 g of product8
4-fluorophenyl-3'-tolylsulfide, Yield 93% m/z 218; C13H11FS requires: C,
71.5; H, 5.08; S, 14.7. Found: C, 71.8; H, 5.38; S, 14.4%; 1H NMR (300
MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.25 (m, 8H), 2.28 (s, 3H); IR (cm-1) νmax; 1591, 1489,
1227.
