$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3,5-Dibromo-2,6-bis(propylthio)aniline (2d). Crude azo An isomeric
mixture of azo derivative 12d (5.0 g, 13.4 mmol) was dissolved in 95%
EtOH (50 mL) with stirring at 70 °C. A solution of NaOH (1.4 g, 35 mmol)
and 1-propanethiol (2.56 g, 34 mmol) in 95% EtOH (15 mL) was added, and
the reaction was stirred overnight at 80 °C. Most of the EtOH was removed
and 6 M HCl (40 mL) was added. The mixture was poured into water (300 mL)
and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and
passed through a silica gel plug (CH2Cl2/hexane, 1:2). The solvent was
then removed to give 13d (6.5 g) as a red-orange oil that was used
without purification for the next step. An analytical sample of 13d was
obtained by column chromatography (CH2Cl2/hexanes, 1:3)
3,5-Dibromo-2,6-bis(propylthio)aniline (2d). Crude azo compound (13d, 6.5
g, 13.3 mmol) was dissolved in AcOH (80 mL), electrolytic grade iron (1
g) was added, and the reaction was stirred at 90 °C overnight. The
reaction mixture was poured into water (300 mL) and extracted with
CH2Cl2. The combined extracts were passed through a silica gel plug
(CH2Cl2). The solvent was removed and the crude product was purified on a
silica gel column (CH2Cl2/hexanes, 1:4) to give amine 2d (3.61 g, 93%
yield from 12d) as an off-white solid. mp 45-46 °C; 1H NMR δ 0.99 (t, J
=7.4 Hz, 6H), 1.58 (sextet, J =7.4 Hz, 4H), 2.74 (t, J =7.3, 4H), 5.79
(br s, 2H), 7.29 (s, 1H); 13C NMR δ 13.5, 23.1, 36.8, 117.1, 124.5,
133.3, 154.1; IR (KBr) 3450 and 3341 (N-H) cm-1; EI-MS m/z 401, 399, 397
(M, 56:100:46). Anal. Calcd for C12H17Br2NS2: C, 36.11; H, 4.29; N, 3.51.
Found: C, 36.37; H, 4.30; N, 3.53.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, intermediate isolated after 2nd stage
