$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-fluorophenyl-4'-methoxyphenylsulfide 4-Bromoanisole (3.35 mL, 26.73
mmol, 1.0 equiv), 2-propanol (30 mL), potassium hydroxide (3.47 g, 53.46
mmol, 2.0 equiv), tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (154 mg,
0.134 mmol, 0.005 equiv), (S)-BINAP (166 mg., 0.267 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and
4-fluorobenzenethiol (2.8 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 22-24 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was
completed it was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (30 mL) which
resulted in a small exotherm (~6 °C) and a formation of an oil. The
reaction slurry so formed, and allowed to stir for 1 hr at 10-15 °C. The
slurry was neutralized using concentrated HCl and extracted with ethyl
acetate, washed with brine and dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered and
concentrated to dryness. Obtained a red oil10, 5.8 g.
4-fluorophenyl-4'-methoxyphenylsulfide, Yield 93% m/z 234; C13H11OS
requires: C, 66.6; H, 4.73; S, 13.7. Found: C, 66.7; H, 4.74; S, 13.7%;
1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.31 (m 4H), 6.96 (m, 4H), 3.82 (s, 6H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Migita reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
