$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed
coupling of aryl chlorides with aromatic thiols: The appropriate quantity
of stock solution B was added to a 4 mL vial containing the aryl chloride
(1.00 mmol) and potasium tert-butoxide (123 mg, 1.10 mmol) in 1.5 mL of
toluene. The aromatic thiol (1.00 mmol) was then added, and the vial
sealed with a cap containing a PTFE septum. The mixture was heated at 110
ºC until the chloroarene was consumed, as determined by GC. Silica gel
(0.5 g) was then added, and solvents were evaporated under reduced
pressure. The crude residue was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane or a mixture of hexane and ethyl acetate as
eluent. Aryl sulfides were isolated in the yields reported in Table 1.
3-Methylphenyl 4-Methylphenyl sulfide (Table 1, entry 15). 8 100 μL of
stock solution B and LiHMDS (184 mg, 1.10 mmol) were used. 93% yield.
Colorless liquid. Colorless liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.28-7.25 (m, 2H),
7.16-7.07 (m, 5H), 6.97 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 2.31 (s, 3H), 2.26 (s, 3H).
13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 138.7, 137.2, 136.5, 131.9 (2C), 131.5, 130.5, 129.9
(2C), 128.8, 127.3, 127.0, 21.2, 21.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A General and Long-Lived Catalyst for the Palladium-Catalyzed Coupling of
Aryl Halides with Thiols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fernandez-Rodriguez, Manuel A.; Shen, Qilong; Hartwig, John F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2006), 128(7), 2180-2181

