$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 3.1. General procedure for the synthesis of 3a-3l In a 25-mL beaker, 5 mL
of IL was placed; then 5 mol% of CuI and 10mol% of Zn(Pro)2 were added
and stirred for0.5 h at 60°C; the mixture was then cooled to room
temperature. This was followed by the addition of 10 mmol of 4-chloro
benzaldehyde, 12 mmol of thiophenol, and 20 mmol of K2CO3 to the IL
mixture, heated to 110°C for 10-16h under nitrogen atmosphere. The cooled
mixture was extracted with ether (15 ml x 3), concentrated under reduced
pressure, and the residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
gel with cyclohexane and ethyl acetate (V: V = 10: 1) as eluent. 3a:
Yellow crystals (from EtOH). Mp: 51-54°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz) δ: 7.25
(d, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H), 7.44 (m, 3H), 7.52 (m, 2H), 7.71 (q, J = 8.6 Hz, J =
4.6 Hz, 2H), 9.91 (s, 1H). IR (KBr) ν: 2750, 1652, 1535, 785 cm-1. 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): 127.33, 129.15, 129.82, 130.13, 131.44, 133.82,
134.34, 147.19, 191.11. MS (70eV) m/z (%): 215 ([M + 2]+, 5.8), 214 (M+,
70), 213 ([M-1]+ 100), 186 (28), 78 (55), 34 (35). Anal, calcd. for
C13H10OS: C 72.87, H 4.70; found C 72.69, H 4.75.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, optimization study, optimized on solvent, base,
temperature and time, ionic liquid support used, reusable catalysts
