$DATUM Synthesis of 3-nitro-4-(p-tolylthio)benzaldehyde 34: A solution of
p-thiocresol (1 g, 5.4 mmol) and 4-chloro-3-nitrobenzaldehyde (0.58 g,
5.4 mmol), NaHCO3 (0.45 g, 5.4 mmol), 3.33 ml water and 6.66 ml ethanol
was heated at reflux for 2 h. After being allowed to cool to room
temperature, the precipitate was filtered out, washed with water and
dried under vacuum. 34 was re-crystallized from acetic acid. Yield: 1.29
g (4,7 mmol), yellow crystals, 92% Elemental Formula: C14H11NO3S,
Molecular Weight: 273.31g mol-1 M.P.: 142°C TLC (petroleum ether : ethyl
acetate, 5:1 ): Rf = 0,4 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 9.95 (s, 1H), 8.67
(d, J = 1.8, 1H), 7.77 (dd, J = 8.5, 1.8, 1H), 7.47-7.43 (m, 2H), 7.31
(d, J = 7.9, 2H), 6.98 (d, J = 8.5, 1H), 2.44 (s, 3H) 13C NMR (101 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 189.26, 148.20, 144.87, 141.52, 136.07, 133.21, 131.90,
131.51, 128.93, 128.04, 126.26, 21.66 CHN analysis: calculated: C: 61.52,
H: 4.06, N: 5.12; found: C: 61.47, H: 4.09, N: 5.24
